  <content>
    <section class="practice" id="sect-00001"><title>Cool Down Activity</title>
      <exercise>
        <problem>
        <para><link class="os-embed" url="#exercise/Alg1_2_3_4_CD_25"/></para>
        </problem>
        </exercise>

      <note id="note-00001">
        <title>Building Character: Growth Mindset</title>
          
            <media alt="Insert Alt Text">
              <image mime-type="image/png" src="../../media/Algebra-1_02_05_09_01.png" width="200px"/>
            </media>
          
            <para id="para-00012">Having a growth mindset means believing you can improve your abilities. Compared
        to a fixed mindset, a growth mindset encourages you to embrace challenges, sustain effort,
        and try new strategies. Think about your current sense of having a growth
        mindset. Are the following statements are true for you?</para>
            <list id="list-00002">
              <item>After I make a mistake, I always look for ways to learn from it. </item>
              <item>I love challenges because they make me smarter. </item>
            </list>
            <para id="para-00013">Don’t
        worry if none of these statements are true for you. Developing this trait takes time. Your
        first step starts today!</para>
      </note>
    </section>
  </content>
